T4 — SageAttention 2.2.0 on the rtx5090 (RTX 5090 Laptop, sm_120). 2026-08-07.

Three renders, one recipe, one seed. Runs 1 and 3 are the NATIVE control and its
repeat; run 2 is the same thing with DIFFUSERS_ATTN_BACKEND set to sage's Triton
kernel. Everything else — venv, harness, prompt files, conditioning still, seed —
is held. Isolated venv C:anyan-bench\sage-venv: sageattention + triton only,
with the production tree's site-packages on sys.path READ-ONLY via a .pth.
C:anyan-videoenv was never written to (verified: it imports neither package).

WHAT WAS INSTALLED, and from where:
  sageattention-2.2.0+cu128torch2.10.0andhigher.post6-cp310-abi3-win_amd64.whl
    github.com/woct0rdho/SageAttention, release v2.2.0-windows.post6 (2026-07-17)
    sha256 103e06df49486daa87c3338bf2490ada2b074da1422f2b90566a8f2f81a6b76e
    — matches the digest GitHub's API publishes for the asset. 16,871,451 bytes.
  triton-windows==3.7.1.post27 (PyPI, 2026-06-21, same maintainer woctordho)
    bundles TinyCC and a minimal CUDA toolchain, so no MSVC and no CUDA toolkit
    were needed — there is no nvcc and no Visual Studio on this box.
  Host: Python 3.12.10, torch 2.11.0+cu128 (RELEASED, not a nightly),
        diffusers 0.39.0, transformers 5.14.1, compute capability (12,0).

